:null,"closed_at":"2026-01-26T18:09:14Z"},"comments":2,"created_at":"2026-01-19T15:31:43Z","updated_at":"2026-01-19T15:49:38Z","closed_at":"2026-01-19T15:49:38Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nGodot Engine v4.6.rc1.official.481f36ed2\n\n### System information\n\nWindows 11 - Godot Engine v4.6.rc1- GPU NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4060 Laptop - CPU 13th Gen Intel(R) Core(TM) i7-13700HX \n\n### Issue description\n\nIn Godot 4.6 RC 1, when selecting a `Skeleton3D` node, the **background rendering layer order of the bones list in the Inspector panel is incorrect**.\nThe specific issues are:\n- The background color blocks of bone entries are rendered with incorrect layer ordering relative to text/UI controls, causing parts of the background to appear on top of text or other UI elements, resulting in visual overlap and blurred content.\n- This issue only affects the visual rendering in the Inspector panel and does not impact the runtime functionality of the `Skeleton3D` node.\n- <img width=\"442\" height=\"1508\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b1437d01-ae51-4f88-b416-4d8c0cf7f6be\" />\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Open Godot 4.6 RC 1.\n2. Create or import a scene containing a `Skeleton3D` node with multiple bones.\n3. Select the `Skeleton3D` node in the Scene Tree.\n4. Observe the bones list in the Inspector panel to see the background layer ordering issue.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[aaaytyy.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/24719172/aaaytyy.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"KoBeWi","id":2223172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjMxNzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2223172?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi",